{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"word embedding word embedding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","fileName":"Word Embedding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Word Embedding","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Natural Language Understanding Systems]] · [[Deep Feature Representation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Deep Feature Representation","Training Dataset","Recurrent Neural Network","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"word embedding word embedding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","fileName":"Word Embedding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Word Embedding","heading":"Word Embedding","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A word embedding represents a word as a dense numerical vector learned from patterns of use. Words that occur in similar contexts tend to receive nearby representations, providing a graded notion of semantic similarity.\n\nUnlike one-hot identifiers, embeddings share statistical information among related words. They give language models and classifiers features that can generalize beyond phrases seen verbatim in a [[Training Dataset]].\n\nKelleher describes word2vec as learning vectors from neighboring-word co-occurrence: words used in similar textual contexts tend to acquire similar vectors. Those vectors can become numerical inputs to a [[Recurrent Neural Network]] for language processing. Proximity reflects patterns in a training corpus; it should not be mistaken for a complete account of a word's meaning in every context.\n\nDeep feature engineering uses these learned vectors as distributed representations rather than sparse word identities. Recurrent, gated, and other sequence models can then operate on dense inputs whose geometry reflects corpus context.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Deep Feature Representation","Training Dataset","Recurrent Neural Network","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"word embedding word embedding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Word Embedding.md","fileName":"Word Embedding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Word Embedding","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]\n\n[[featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Deep Feature Representation","Training Dataset","Recurrent Neural Network","aiassistants.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}